cellAdec: AC3 through FFmpeg loaded at run time; real AC3 frame sizes when FFmpeg is absent.

Symptom (Killzone 2 1.29, intro movie MOVIES/GameIntro_PS3.avi, AC3 5.1 at 448 kb/s, 1792-byte AUs): the stub gave
every AU 1024 stereo float samples of silence (8192 bytes in the PcmItem size and in bsiInfo+0x14). KZ2's movie
player sizes its PCM ring as channels x 4 bytes a sample (audio display +0x2D4 = 6 << 2, set at 0xA07EC0) and takes
each AU's PCM size from bsiInfo+0x14 (PCMOUT handler 0xA042D0, flag path 0xA045F8), so it fed its 5.1 mixer 341
sample frames per AU instead of 1536, and silence even where a decoder could have been loaded.

Fix:
- AC3 (codecType 2) decodes through libavcodec when PS3RECOMP_FFMPEG_RUNTIME is built in and FFmpeg loads
  (ps3_ffmpeg_get(), the loader cellVdec uses; no new FFmpeg functions). The PCM is the frame's samples in the
  decoder's channel order (FFmpeg's native order, for 5.1 L R C LFE Ls Rs), interleaved big-endian float; one
  1536-sample frame per AU, its size in the PcmItem and bsiInfo+0x14. cellAdecGetPcm copies that block to the
  title's buffer. StartSeq flushes the decoder, Close frees it.
- The AU bytes and AU info are copied before AUDONE, which hands the AU buffer back to the title's demuxer.
- Without a decoder (no FFmpeg, PS3RECOMP_FFMPEG=0, a damaged AU) AC3 gives silence of the real frame size:
  1536 samples in the frame's channels from its header (acmod + lfeon, A/52 5.4.2; 2 when it is not an AC3 frame).
  Other codec types keep the old 1024-sample stereo silence.
- The PCM block (up to 1536 x 8 x 4 = 48 KB) moves from the 16 KB per-handle scratch to its own 64 KB per handle at
  VM_HLE_INJECT_BASE + 0x80000..0xC0000 (clear of every other user of the window).

Verification: tools/runtime/test_adec_ac3.sh (host; stub sizes 36864/12288/8192 without FFmpeg and with
PS3RECOMP_FFMPEG=0; with host libavcodec 63 every AU of a 5.1 stream equals FFmpeg's own decode sample for sample,
and swapped channels or a dropped AU are caught); Killzone 2 under Proton (the RE notes, 2026-10-22: real AC3 frames).
Upstream candidate (general: AC3 movie audio, and the real frame size for any title that sizes PCM from bsiInfo).
Written for this port; FFmpeg is not copied, only called (LGPL-2.1-or-later, separate DLLs).

